  "id": "ENT005",
  "title": "The Umbrella Under the Rain",
  "family": "fiction",
  "category": "physical comedy",
  "premise": "A figure tries to keep one tiny flower dry with an umbrella, but water collected on the canopy repeatedly tips onto the flower. The figure turns the umbrella into a distant catch basin and gives the flower a small flat roof, then gets drenched while celebrating.",
  "hook": "One flower. One umbrella. Terrible management.",
  "visible_action": "Umbrella tilts; water sloshes; flower ducks on a flexible stem; canopy flips into a bowl away from the flower; a tiny roof unfolds.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "A tool can solve one problem while creating another.",
  "gate": "Cartoon water and plant behavior; no claim that flowers need rain protection or that the build is weather-safe.",
  "evidence_class": "fictional_demonstration",
